# Step 2: Analyze

@read-frontmatter path="state.stage" label="state" /

@assert operator="json-key" target="state.stage" key="step" equals="1" /
@assert operator="json-key" target="state.stage" key="run_id" equals="{{ vars.run_id }}" /

@if state.step !== "1"
**BLOCKED (skipped-step).** Step 2 requires step 1 to have completed first.
Current state: step={{ state.step }}, run_id={{ state.run_id }}. Run
01-collect.stage --var run_id={{ vars.run_id }} before this step.
@else
@if state.run_id !== vars.run_id
**BLOCKED (stale-state).** state.stage belongs to a different run
({{ state.run_id }}), not the run in progress ({{ vars.run_id }}).
Refusing to trust it rather than silently analyzing the wrong run's data.
@else
Analyzing collected data for run {{ vars.run_id }}...

@update-frontmatter path="state.stage" field="step" value="2" /
@update-frontmatter path="state.stage" field="updated_at" value="{{ now_iso() }}" /

Step 2 complete. State now reflects run {{ vars.run_id }}, step 2.
@if-end
@if-end
